{
 "answer": "Watcher wake signal is class-specific: canonical content-hash for HTML and plain specs, entry-id set for feeds and VCS atoms, release-tag set for releases.atom, version plus file digests for registries. ETag and Last-Modified are cheap prechecks; they do not wake HTML by themselves. Both-states control passed=True: genuine edits wake; ad/timestamp/lastBuildDate/published_at-only edits do not. A raw-byte poller wakes on both plants. Live paired sample n=20 over 9.1s of real elapsed time (not a mutated local copy): watcher false-wake rate=0.0, poller false-wake rate=0.0. Source-native timestamps in those payloads counted 109 load-bearing events in the prior 7 UTC days (true-wake opportunities). A standing 7-day daemon was not run. A wake appends a WatchEvent and enqueues claim revalidation only for claims citing that source_id; it does not refetch the rest of the watchlist. SUCCESS:RES-0180",
